nt\nimplementation of the Official Language Policy for the\nyear 2024–25.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nZonal Office, Varanasi has been awarded the ‘First Prize’ for outstanding","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c727","section":"Management Discussion & Analysis","tag":"mdna","page":324,"text":"Zonal Office, Varanasi has been awarded the ‘First Prize’ for outstanding\nperformance in the implementation of Official Language Hindi.\nZonal Office, Kolkata (North) has been awarded the ‘First Prize’ for Outstanding\nperformance in the implementation of Official Language Hindi.\nZonal Office, Patna has been awarded ‘Second Prize’ for outstanding\nperformance in the implementation of Official Language Hindi.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nIndian Bank, Corporate Office has been conferred with the ‘NARAKAS Rajbhasha\nSamman’ (Third Prize – Region ‘C’) as the convenor bank of the Town Official\nLanguage Implementation Committee (Banks/Financial Institutions), Chennai by\nthe Department of Official Language, Ministry of Home Affairs, Government of\nIndia, for outstanding implementation of the Official Language Policy during the\nfinancial year 2024–25.\nBank was honoured with ‘First Prize’ in ‘Region C’ at a grand event organized in Udaipur by the Department of Financial\nServices, Ministry of Finance, Government of India in recognition of the effective implementation of the Official\nLanguage Policy and excellent performance during the financial year 2025–26.\n28. AWARDS & ACCOLADES\nCEO of the Year at TN Business Leader of the Year 2025\nBank won Prestigious SKOCH Golden Award for IB SAATHI & SKOCH Silver Award for Security Operations\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c728","section":"Management Discussion & Analysis","tag":"mdna","page":326,"text":"2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nBank has received IBEX India 2026\nET Edge BFSI Tech Leaders Award -\nBFSI Tech Award (Bronze) under\nArchitects of Bharat’s Financial Future\nDigital CX Trailblazer - PSU\nDigital Leadership Award at\n5th Edition of “Connect Future Ready Leaders Viksit Bharat 2047” by Enqube Collaborations\nVMware – India Cloud Leader Award 2025\nBank has received Special Mention under Best IT Risk\nDigital Payments Awards 2023-24\nManagement &\nFrom Ministry of Finance\nBest Technology Bank at IBA’s 21st Annual Banking\nTechnology Conference 2024-25\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n29. REGIONAL RURAL BANKS (RRBs):\n• The Bank has two sponsored Regional Rural Banks viz., Tamil Nadu Grama Bank (TNGB) headquartered at Salem\n(Tamil Nadu) and Puducherry Grama Bank headquartered at Puducherry (Union Territory of Puducherry).\n• Saptagiri Grameena Bank (SGB) has since been merged with Andhra Pradesh Grameena Bank sponsored by Union\nBank, w.e.f. 01.05.25.\n• As per the notification issued by the Central Government on 23.10.25 under the Regional Rural Banks Act, 1976, the\nbank formerly known as Puduvai Bharathiyar Grama Bank has been renamed as Puducherry Grama Bank.\n• In respect of two RRBs, the branch network has increased by 25 from 722 (March 2025) to 747 Branches (March 2026).","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c729","section":"Management Discussion & Analysis","tag":"mdna","page":327,"text":"• In respect of two RRBs, the branch network has increased by 25 from 722 (March 2025) to 747 Branches (March 2026).\nThe total business of the two RRBs was ₹61,968 Crore as on 31.03.26 as compared to ₹53,924 Crore as on 31.03.25\n(YoY growth of 15%).\n• Both RRBs are profit making.\nBusiness position as on 31.03.2026 (Audited) (₹ in Cr)\nNet NPA\nS. No. Name of the RRB No. of Branches Deposits Advances Business Net Profit\n% CRAR %\n1 Tamil Nadu Grama Bank 699 26232 31735 57966 623 0 13.34\n2 Puducherry Grama Bank 48 1923 2079 4002 60 0 10.39\nTotal 747 28155 33814 61968 683 0 -\n• RRBs are actively participating in the Government of India’s financial inclusion schemes such as PMJDY, PMJJBY, PMSBY,\nand APY. As on 31.03.26, they have 13.76 lakh PMJDY accounts, covered 9.71 lakh beneficiaries under PMJJBY, 18.89\nlakh beneficiaries under PMSBY, and 4.17 lakh beneficiaries under APY.\n30. SUBSIDIARIES AND JOINT VENTURES\nUniversal Sompo General Insurance (P) Limited:\n• The Bank has a joint venture with a Consortium of Public & Private Corporate entities from India and Sompo of Japan\nas promoters and was incorporated in 2007.\n• Universal Sompo General Insurance Co. Ltd. is a joint venture of Indian Bank, Indian Overseas Bank, Karnataka Bank\nLtd., Dabur Investment Corporation and a leading general insurer from Japan, Sompo Japan Insurance Inc. It offers a","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c730","section":"Management Discussion & Analysis","tag":"mdna","page":327,"text":"Ltd., Dabur Investment Corporation and a leading general insurer from Japan, Sompo Japan Insurance Inc. It offers a\nwide-range of products catering to Retail, Rural, SME & Corporate customer segments.\n• As on 31.03.26, the Indian Bank’s shareholding was at 28.52%\n• The Net Profit has been ₹226 Crore in FY26 as against ₹190 Crore in FY25 registering a growth of 18.95%.\nIndbank Merchant Banking Services Limited:\nThe subsidiary functions across corporate, retail, and institutional financial segments through the following core\noperational wings:\n• Merchant Banking: Undertakes capital market assignments as Lead Manager, Co-Manager, Advisor, or Arranger for\nPublic Issues, Rights Issues, and Private Placements. They also manage buybacks, delistings, and corporate share\ntakeovers under SEBI guidelines.\n• Stock Broking: Corporate member of the NSE and BSE. They offer retail and institutional online trading platforms\n(IndFortune) spanning Equity, Derivatives (F&O), and ETFs.\n• Depository Participant (DP) Services: Registered with both NSDL and CDSL to handle demat accounts and electronic\nholding transactions for retail and corporate clients.\n• Investment Distribution: Regulated AMFI mutual fund distributor utilizing their IndWealth platform for regular and\nsystemic investment plans (SIPs)\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n• The company is listed on NSE and BSE","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c731","section":"Management Discussion & Analysis","tag":"mdna","page":328,"text":"• The company is listed on NSE and BSE\n• As on 31.03.26, the Bank’s shareholding was at 64.84%.\n• The subsidiary witnessed Net Profit of ₹7.09 Crore in FY26 and earned income of ₹14.11 Crore under stock broking.\nIndBank Global Support Services Limited (IGSSL):\n• IGSSL is a Wholly Owned Subsidiary (WOS) of Indian Bank, incorporated on 09.02.24 with an authorized and paid-up\nCapital of ₹10 Crore to offer comprehensive outsourcing solutions for various banking operations as permitted by\nRBI. The WOS is active in garnering deposits, sourcing mortgage, vehicle loans, improving digital penetration and\nrecovery. The subsidiary witnessed Net Profit of ₹28 lakh in FY26.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nINTENTIONALLY LEFT BLANK\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nExclusive Salary Account\n*T&C Apply\nfor Central Government\nPermanent Employees\nFree Insurance Coverage up to ₹2.07 Cr\nFree Healthcare consultation for self and\n4 family members\nFree debit card with lifestyle privileges\nScan to know more\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY20