are Transfer Committee\n10. HR Committee\n11. Committee for Monitoring of Recovery\n12. Credit Approval Committee\n13. Committee of Directors (Capital Raising)\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n1. Committee of Directors (Vigilance)\n2. Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow-up of cases of Frauds\nGovt. Nominee Director\n3. IT Strategy Committee\n6. Dr. Alok Pande\n13.05.2024\nITC Ltd. -\n4. HR Committee\n5. Committee for Monitoring of Recovery\n6. Board Committee for Performance Evaluation (Chairman)\n1. Management Committee","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c738","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":336,"text":"1. Management Committee\n2. Audit Committee of the Board\n7. Smt. K. Nikhila\nRBI Nominee Director 14.07.2023\n- -\n3. Committee of Directors (Vigilance)\n1. Audit Committee of the Board\n2. Customer Service Committee\n3. Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow –up of cases of Frauds (Chairman)\n4. IT Strategy Committee\nPart-time Non Official Director\n8. Shri Balmukund Sahay\n11.04.2025\n- -\n5. Stakeholders Relationship Committee (Chairman)\n6. Committee for Monitoring of Recovery\n7. Board Level Appellate Committee for Disciplinary cases (Chairman)\n8. Nomination and Remuneration Committee (Chairman)\n1. Management Committee\n2. Customer Service Committee\n3. Risk Management Committee (Chairman)\n4. IT Strategy Committee\n5. HR Committee\n9. Shri Vishvesh Kumar Goel\nPart-time Non Official Director\nV G Corporate Management Pvt Ltd\n6. Committee for Monitoring of Recovery\n11.04.2025\n-\n7. Board Level Appellate Committee for Disciplinary cases\n8. Review Committee for Wilful Defaulters\n9. Nomination and Remuneration Committee\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n1. Audit Committee of the Board (Chairman)\n2. Risk Management Committee\n3. Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow –up of cases of Frauds\n• Trust AMC Trustees Private Limited\n4. Share Transfer Committee\n10. Shri Sanjeev Maheshwari\nShareholder Director 21.12.2024","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c739","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":337,"text":"Shareholder Director 21.12.2024\n• MSSBL Traders Limited (converted to LLP w.e.f. 03/02/2024)\n5. Board Level Appellate Committee for Disciplinary cases\n6. Review Committee for Wilful Defaulters\n7. Nomination and Remuneration Committee\n8. Board Committee for Performance Evaluation\n1. Audit Committee of the Board\n2. Risk Management Committee\n3. IT Strategy Committee (Chairman)\n11. Shri Bhupinder Singh Bhalla\nShareholder Director 31.12.2025\n- 150\n4. Stakeholders Relationship Committee\n5. Share Transfer Committee\n6. Nomination and Remuneration Committee\n7. Board Committee for Performance Evaluation\nNote:\n(i) None of the directors on the Board is member in more than 10 committees namely Audit Committee and Stakeholders’\nRelationship Committee or act as Chairman of more than 5 Committees namely Audit Committee and Stakeholders’\nRelationship Committee across all companies in which he/she is a director.\n(ii) There is no inter-se relationship between Directors.\n(iii) Details of familiarization programmes imparted to independent Directors are available on Bank’s website under the\nlink, https://indianbank.bank.in/departments/corporate-governance-2/\n(iv) The Board of Directors has been responsible for the business and overall affairs of the Bank in the FY 2025-26 and that\nthe reporting structures of the Bank, formal and informal are in consistent with the same.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c740","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":337,"text":"the reporting structures of the Bank, formal and informal are in consistent with the same.\n(v) In the opinion of the Board, the independent directors fulfill the conditions specified in SEBI (LODR) regulations, 2015\nand are independent of the management.\n(vi) During FY 2025-26, there has been only one instance of resignation by one Independent Director, Shri Pradeep Kumar\nMalhotra, Shareholder Director. Shri Pradeep Kumar Malhotra submitted his resignation vide letter dated 28.11.2025\npursuant to RBl's communication dated 30.07.2025 disqualifying serving employees of Life Insurance Corporation of\nIndia being connected with para banking activities to be on the Board of PSBs as Shareholder Director in terms of para\n4.3(iv)(b) of Master Direction-Reserve Bank of India ('Fit & Proper' Criteria for Elected Directors on the Board of PSBs)\nDirections, 2019 dated August 02, 2019 (updated as on June 03, 2020). Accordingly Shri Pradeep Kumar Malhotra\nceased to be a Director of the Bank w.e.f. 28.11.2025.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n(vii) Shri Ashutosh Choudhury, Executive Director attended meeting of Audit Committee of the Board as invitee.\n(viii) Shri Shiv Bajrang Singh, Executive Director attended meeting of Audit Committee and Risk Management Committee\nof the Board as invitee.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c741","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":338,"text":"of the Board as invitee.\n(ix) Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh, Executive Director attended meeting of Audit Committee and Risk Management Committee\nof the Board as invitee.\n(x) Ms. Mini T M, Executive Director attended meeting of Audit Committee and Risk Management Committee of the\nBoard as invitee\n2.5 The profiles of the directors who were appointed / nominated on the Board of the Bank and assumed office\nduring the financial year 2025-26 are furnished hereunder:\n2.5.1. Ms. Mini T M, Executive Director:\nMs. Mini T M is a highly accomplished banking professional with more than three decades of wide-ranging experience\nacross Federal Bank, e-Vijaya Bank, and Bank of Baroda. She joined Indian Bank as Executive Director, bringing with her\na distinguished record of leading large business portfolios, driving strategic growth and strengthening governance\nand risk frameworks at scale. In her most recent role as Chief General Manager & Cluster Head Delhi at Bank of\nBaroda, Ms. Mini oversaw a business portfolio of approximately Rs. 6.00 lakh crore, providing strategic direction\nacross deposits, advances, customer service, and compliance. Prior to this, she headed the pan-India Retail Liabilities\nvertical, spearheading product innovation, digital enhancements, and sustained growth in CASA and term deposits.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c742","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":338,"text":"vertical, spearheading product innovation, digital enhancements, and sustained growth in CASA and term deposits.\nHer leadership journey includes heading major Zones such as Bengaluru and Pune, where she delivered strong\nbusiness expansion, improved asset quality, enhanced customer experience and introduced multiple governance and\ndigital transformation initiatives. She has also led PSU and corporate business for the southern region and previously\nheld senior responsibilities in credit, SME banking, corporate credit operations and risk management. Ms. Mini holds\nan MBA in Banking & Finance, is an FRM (GARP, USA), a CAIIB and has completed premier leadership programs at\nIIM Ahmedabad, IIM Bangalore, CAFRAL, and international leadership forums. Recognized for her strategic clarity,\noperational excellence and people-centric leadership, Ms. Mini has consistently contributed towards building strong,\nfuture-ready banking ecosystems and delivering sustainable growth across diverse business segments.\n2.5.2. Shri Bhupinder Singh Bhalla, Shareholder Director:\nWith an honours degree from Shri Ram College of Commerce, ICWA and a PGDM (MBA) from the Indian Institute of\nManagement, Bangalore, Shri Bhupinder Singh Bhalla worked in corporate finance for three years before joining the","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c743","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":338,"text":"Management, Bangalore, Shri Bhupinder Singh Bhalla worked in corporate finance for three years before joining the\nIndian Administrative Service (IAS) in 1990. Till recently, he was working as Technical Member, Appellate Tribunal for\nElectricity, Government of India. Earlier, as the Secretary of the Ministry of New and Renewable Energy till he retired in\nSep 2024, he was responsible for driving India’s energy transition through massive scale-up of the renewable energy\nsector. His notable accomplishments include launch of the National Green Hydrogen Mission and the PM Surya Ghar:\nMuft Bijli Yojana; impetus to solar manufacturing; and kick-starting the offshore wind development in the country.\nHe has also worked at other key positions at the Government of India. As Joint Secretary, and then as Additional\nSecretary, Ministry of Commerce & Industry for over five years, he was responsible for India’s trade negotiations with\nthe neighbouring countries. In addition, he worked as Director General, Trade Remedies and led the India Brand Equity\nFoundation as its CEO. He has also worked as Counsellor (Economic) in the Indian Embassy at Washington DC, USA where\nhe spearheaded the India-US bilateral engagements in finance, energy and agriculture for over three years. Earlier, as","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c744","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":338,"text":"he spearheaded the India-US bilateral engagements in finance, energy and agriculture for over three years. Earlier, as\nDirector, Department of Financial Services Ministry of Finance, he played a role in several major initiatives in India’s\nbanking sector, and served as Government Nominee Director on the board of Union Bank of India from 24 January 2005\nto 10 June 2008. As a member of the Union Territory cadre of the IAS, he has had memorable stints in diverse fields\nacross Delhi, Goa, Daman & Diu, Andaman & Nicobar Islands and Chandigarh, including as the Administrator, Union\nTerritories of Daman & Diu and Dadra & Nagar Haveli, where he served as the constitutional and administrative head.\nAs a Fellow Member of the Institute of Cost Accountants of India, he has been conferred with the inaugural CMA Ratna\nAward 2016 by the Institute for significant contribution to the cause of society and the profession as a policymaker.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n2.5.3. Shri Balmukund Sahay, Part Time Non Official Director:\nShri Balmukund Sahay is a post graduate in Commerce from Ranchi University.\nHe was an active member of Jharkhand State Transport Authority from 2001 to 2004 and member of Jharkhand State\nLevel 20 Points Programme Committee from 2016 to 2019. As a member of Jharkhand State Transport Authority, he","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c745","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":339,"text":"Level 20 Points Programme Committee from 2016 to 2019. As a member of Jharkhand State Transport Authority, he\nhad a role to promote rural economy and improve transportation sector.\nHe is a social activist and as a member of Jharkhand State Level 20 Points Programme Committee, he was focusing\non encouraging Agriculture, Rural Economy, Small Scale Industries & Information Technology and alternative dispute\nresolution. Poverty alleviation, facilitating government schemes to beneficiaries, were also his subject of interest.\n2.5.4. Shri Vishvesh Kumar Goel, Part Time Non Official Director\nHe is a member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants of India and holds Bachelor degree in Commerce from\nMeerut University. He has experience of more than 30 years in direct taxation, international transaction advisory,\nLegal opinions, Expatriate Taxation, etc. He also has extensive experience in Assurance Services & serving listed\nIndian and Multinational clients in various industries.\nHe has worked under various GAAPs (including USGAAP, IFRS, Ind AS, etc.). He is founder trustee of Eminent Educational\nInstitute. He is an active participant in public seminars on direct taxation, training and other motivational programs.\n2.6 The details of cessation of directorship during FY 2025-26 are as under:\nSl. No. Name Category Date of cessation Reason\n1. Shri Mahesh Kumar Bajaj Executive","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c746","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":339,"text":"1. Shri Mahesh Kumar Bajaj Executive\nDirector 01.07.2025 Completion of term of appointment\n2. Shri Pradeep Kumar Malhotra Shareholder\nDirector 28.11.2025 Resignation\n3. Credentials of members of Board of Directors (as on 31.03.2026):\nEducational/ Professional\nSl. No. Name Designation Category of\nQualification Skill/ Expertise\nDirector\nB.Sc.(H), Post Graduate Diploma in Banking & Finance, Financial Risk Manager, Diploma in Banking & Finance, Diploma in Treasury, Investment & Risk Management, CAIIB\n1. Shri Binod Kumar MD & CEO Executive\nBanker\nMBA, Executive Leadership Development Program from IIM Bangalore\nExecutive\n2. Shri Ashutosh Choudhury\nBanker\nDirector Executive\nMA, MBA, CAIIB, Certificate in Rural Banking, Leadership Development Programme for Senior Management of Public Sector Banks at IIM Bangalore\nExecutive\n3. Shri Shiv Bajrang Singh\nBanker\nDirector Executive\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nEducational/ Professional\nSl. No. Name Designation Category of\nQualification Skill/ Expertise\nDirector\nB.Sc. (Agri), MBA (Finance), CAIIB, Leadership Development Programme for Senior Management of Public Sector Banks at IIM Bangalore\nExecutive\n4. Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh\nBanker\nDirector Executive\nB.Sc (Agriculture), MBA (Banking & Finance), CAIIB, FRM (GARP, USA) Post Graduate Diploma in Financial Management\n5. Ms. Mini T M Executive\nBanker\nDirector Executive","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c747","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":340,"text":"Director Executive\nGovt. Service, Additional Secretary, Department of Investment and Public Asset Management (DIPAM) , Ministry of Finance\nNon Executive-\nB.E. (Mechanical), FPM (Doctorate)\n6. Dr. Alok Pande GOI Nominee\nGOI Nominee\nDirector\nDirector\nChief General Manager-in-Charge, RBI, Premises Department\nNon Executive-\nM.Sc., Certified Associate of IIB&F\n7. Smt. K. Nikhila RBI Nominee\nRBI Nominee\nDirector\nDirector\nNon Executive-\n8. Shri Balmukund Sahay\nPart-Time Non Official Director\nIndependent\nM.Com. Social Activist\nDirector\nNon Executive-\nB. Com., CA Practicing Chartered Accountant\n9. Shri Vishvesh Kumar Goel\nPart-Time Non Official Director\nIndependent\nDirector\nNon Executive-\nB. Com. (Hons) FCA, DISA\nPracticing Chartered Accountant\nShareholder\n10. Shri Sanjeev Maheshwari\nIndependent\nDirector\nDirector\nNon Executive-\nShareholder\n11. Shri Bhupinder Singh Bhalla\nB. Com. (Hons.), ICWA, PGDM, MBA\nRetired IAS Officer/ Cost Accountant\nIndependent\nDirector\nDirector\n3.1 Details of the Board / Committee meeting held during financial year 2025-26:\nDetails of the meetings attended by Present and Past Directors (fro