749","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":341,"text":"Number of Directors Attended\nSl. No. Date of meeting Number of Directors on\nBoard\nthe meeting\n1 26.04.2025 & 27.04.2025 * (Strategy Board) 11 10\n2 03.05.2025 11 11\n3 19.05.2025 11 10\n4 26.06.2025 11 10\n5 24.07.2025 10 9\n6 26.09.2025 10 9\n7 26.09.2025 (Seq Board) # 10 9\n8 16.10.2025 10 10\n9 22.11.2025 & 23.11.2025** (Strategy Board) 10 10\n10 29.12.2025 & 30.12.2025* (Strategy Board) 10 8\n11 22.01.2026 11 10\n12 06.03.2026 11 10\n13 06.03.2026 (Seq Board) # 11 10\n14 27.03.2026 11 10\n* Strategy Board Meeting started on 26.04.2025 and ended on 27.04.2025\n** Strategy Board Meeting started on 22.11.2025 and ended on 23.11.2025\n# Board has sequence Board meeting on 26.09.2025 & 06.03.2026\n4. Committees of the Board:\nThe Board has constituted various committees as mentioned hereunder for specific and focused approach towards\ngovernance of some of the important functional areas of the Bank, for providing proper direction, effective monitoring\nand controlling the affairs of the Bank:\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n(i) Management Committee of the Board (MCB)\n(ii) Audit Committee of the Board (ACB)\n(iii) Risk Management Committee (RMC)\n(iv) IT Strategy Committee (ITSC)\n(v) Customer Service Committee (CSC)\n(vi) Committee of Directors (Vigilance) (COD Vig)\n(vii) Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow-up of cases of Frauds (SCBMF)","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c750","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":342,"text":"(vii) Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow-up of cases of Frauds (SCBMF)\n(viii) Share Transfer Committee (STC)\n(ix) Stakeholders Relationship Committee (SRC)\n(x) H R Committee (HR Com)\n(xi) Committee for Monitoring of Recovery (CMR)\n(xii) Board Level Appellate Committee for Disciplinary Cases (BACDC)\n(xiii) Review Committee for Wilful Defaulters (RCWD)\n(xiv) Credit Approval Committee (CAC)\n(xv) Nomination and Remuneration Committee (NRC)\n(xvi) Board Committee for Performance Evaluation (BCPE)\n(xvii) Committee of Directors (Capital Raising) (COD Capital Raising)\n4.1 Management Committee of the Board:\nThe Management Committee was constituted on September 8, 1990 and exercises such powers of the Board, as may\nbe delegated to it by the Board with the approval of the Central Government after consultation with Reserve Bank of\nIndia. The committee is re-constituted from time to time. The Management Committee may exercise all the powers\nvested in the Board in respect of:\n• Sanctioning of credit proposals (funded and non-funded);\n• Loans compromise/write-off proposals;\n• Proposals for approval of capital and revenue expenditure;\n• Proposals relating to acquisition and hiring of premises including deviation from norms for acquisition and hiring\nof premises;\n• Investments in Government and other approved securities, shares and debentures of companies including","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c751","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":342,"text":"• Investments in Government and other approved securities, shares and debentures of companies including\nunderwriting;\n• Donations, and\n• Any other matter referred to the Management Committee by the Board\n4.1.1 Composition of the Management Committee of the Board:\nThe members of the Management Committee of the Board as on 31.03.2026 were as under:\nSl. No. Name Chairman/Member\n1 Shri Binod Kumar, MD & CEO Chairman\n2 Shri Ashutosh Choudhury, Executive Director Member\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n3 Shri Shiv Bajrang Singh, Executive Director Member\n4 Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh, Executive Director Member\n5 Ms. Mini T M, Executive Director Member\n6 Ms. K Nikhila, RBI Nominee Director Member\n7 Shri Vishvesh Kumar Goel, Part Time Non-Official Director Member\n4.1.2 Details of meetings:\nThe Committee met 24 times during the period from 01.04.2025 to 31.03.2026 as detailed below:\nNumber of Directors Attended\nSl. No. Date of meeting Number of Directors on the Management\nCommittee of Board\nthe meeting\n1 11.04.2025 6 5\n2 30.04.2025 7 7\n3 14.05.2025 7 6\n4 30.05.2025 7 7\n5 12.06.2025 7 7\n6 25.06.2025 7 7\n7 27.06.2025 7 7\n8 23.07.2025 6 6\n9 31.07.2025 6 5\n10 12.08.2025 6 6\n11 29.08.2025 6 6\n12 15.09.2025 6 6\n13 24.09.2025 6 5\n14 26.09.2025 6 6\n15 30.10.2025 6 6\n16 14.11.2025 6 6\n17 29.11.2025 7 7\n18 15.12.2025 7 6\n19 29.12.2025 7 5\n20 27.01.2026 7 6\n21 16.02.2026 7 6","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c752","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":343,"text":"21 16.02.2026 7 6\n22 26.02.2026 7 6\n23 18.03.2026 7 6\n24 27.03.2026 7 7\n4.2 Audit Committee of the Board (ACB):\nThe Audit Committee was constituted on October 13, 1995 and the same is re-constituted from time to time. Its terms\nof reference include the following:\n• Provide direction as also oversee the total audit function of the Bank which impact the organization,\noperationalization and quality control of internal audit and inspection in the Bank and follow-up on the statutory/\nexternal audit of the Bank and inspections of the Reserve Bank of India.\n• Review the internal inspection/audit function in the Bank, with specific focus on the follow-up on inter-branch\nadjustment accounts, un-reconciled long outstanding entries in Inter-Bank accounts and nostro accounts,\narrears in balancing of books at various branches, frauds and house-keeping.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n• Review quarterly reports from the Compliance officers appointed in the Bank\n• Follow-up on all the issues raised in the Long form Audit Report and interact with the external auditors before\nthe finalization of the annual/semi-annual financial accounts and reports and all the issues/concerns raised in\nthe inspection reports of RBI.\n• Regular review of accounts, accounting policies, disclosures.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c753","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":344,"text":"• Regular review of accounts, accounting policies, disclosures.\n• Review of the major accounting entries based on exercise of judgment by management and review of significant\nadjustments arising out of audit.\n• Qualifications in the draft audit report.\n• Establishing and reviewing the scope of the independent audit including the observations of the auditors and\nreview of the quarterly, half-yearly and annual financial statements before submission to the Board.\n• Post audit discussions with the auditors to ascertain any area of concern.\n• Establishing the scope and frequency of internal audit, reviewing the findings of the internal auditors and\nensuring the adequacy of internal control systems.\n• Compliance with Accounting Standards and Accounting Policies of the Bank.\n• Compliance with stock exchange requirements concerning financial statements, to the extent applicable.\n• Oversee related party transactions i.e., transactions of the Bank of material nature, with promoters or\nmanagement, their subsidiaries or relatives etc., that may have potential conflict with the interests of the Bank\nat large and\n• Such other matters as may from time to time be required by any statutory, contractual or other regulatory\nrequirements\n4.2.1 Composition of the Audit Committee of the Board:\nThe members of Audit Committee of the Board as on 31.03.2026 were as under:\nSl. No. Name Chairman/Member","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c754","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":344,"text":"Sl. No. Name Chairman/Member\n1 Shri Sanjeev Maheshwari, Shareholder Director Chairman\n2 Ms. K Nikhila, RBI Nominee Director Member\n3 Shri Balmukund Sahay, Part time Non Official Director Member\n4 Shri Bhupinder Singh Bhalla, Shareholder Director Member\nInvitees:\n(i) Shri Ashutosh Choudhury, Executive Director\n(ii) Shri Shiv Bajrang Singh, Executive Director\n(iii) Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh, Executive Director\n(iv) Ms. Mini T M, Executive Director\n4.2.2 Details of meetings:\nDuring the period from 01.04.2025 to 31.03.2026, 12 meetings of the Audit committee of the Board were held as\ndetailed below:\nNumber of Directors Attended\nSl. No. Date of meeting Number of Directors on the Audit\nCommittee of Board\nthe meeting\n1 03.05.2025 4 4\n2 09.06.2025 4 3\n3 18.06.2025 4 3\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n4 24.07.2025 4 3\n5 18.09.2025 4 3\n6 16.10.2025 4 4\n7 04.11.2025 4 4\n8 18.11.2025 4 3\n9 09.12.2025 3 3\n10 22.01.2026 4 3\n11 13.02.2026 4 4\n12 23.03.2026 4 3\n4.3 Risk Management Committee of the Board:\nRisk Management Committee was constituted on January 18, 2003 and the committee was re-constituted from time\nto time. The functions/ responsibilities of the Risk Management Committee include the following:\n• To devise the policy and strategy for integrated risk management containing various risk exposures of the Bank\nincluding the Credit Risk.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c755","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":345,"text":"including the Credit Risk.\n• To co-ordinate between the Credit Risk Management Committee (CRMC), the Asset Liability Management\nCommittee (ALMC) and Operational Risk Management Committee (ORMC) and other risk committees of the\nBank.\n• Setting policies and guidelines for market risk measurement, management and reporting.\n• Ensuring that market risk management processes (including people, systems, operations, limits and controls)\nsatisfy Bank’s policy.\n• Reviewing and approving market risk limits, including triggers or stop-losses for traded and accrual portfolios.\n• Appointment of qualified and competent staff, ensuring posting of qualified and competent staff and of\nindependent market risk manager/s etc.\n4.3.1 Composition of the Risk Management Committee of the Board:\nThe members of Risk Management Committee of the Board as on 31.03.2026 were as under:\nSl. No. Name Chairman/Member\n1 Shri Vishvesh Kumar Goel, Part time Non Official Director Chairman\n2 Shri Binod Kumar, MD & CEO Member\n3 Shri Ashutosh Choudhury, Executive Director Member\n4 Shri Sanjeev Maheshwari, Shareholder Director Member\n5 Shri Bhupinder Singh Bhalla, Shareholder Director Member\nInvitees:\n(i) Shri Shiv Bajrang Singh, Executive Director\n(ii) Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh, Executive Director\n(iii) Ms. Mini T M, Executive Director\n(iv) Shri Himadri Bhattacharya, domain expert (Special Invitee)","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c756","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":346,"text":"(iv) Shri Himadri Bhattacharya, domain expert (Special Invitee)\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n4.3.2 Details of meetings:\nThe Committee met 6 times during the period from 01.04.2025 to 31.03.2026 as detailed below:\nNumber of Directors Attended the\nSl. No. Date of meeting Number of Directors on the Risk Management Committee of Board\nmeeting\n1 14.05.2025 5 4\n2 18.06.2025 5 5\n3 11.09.2025 5 5\n4 19.12.2025 5 5\n5 19.02.2026 5 5\n6 18.03.2026 5 5\n4.4 Committee of Directors (COD) on Vigilance:\nThe Vigilance Committee was constituted on January 12, 1991. The Vigilance Committee meets once in a quarter to\nreview any outstanding disciplinary cases and departmental enquiries. The Committee was reconstituted from time\nto time.\n4.4.1 Composition of the Committee of Directors (COD) on Vigilance:\nThe members of Committee of Directors (COD) on Vigilance as on 31.03.2026 were as under:\nSl. No. Name Chairman/Member\n1 Shri Binod Kumar, MD & CEO Chairman\n2 Shri Ashutosh Choudhury, Executive Director Member\n3 Shri Shiv Bajrang Singh, Executive Director Member\n4 Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh, Executive Director Member\n5 Ms. Mini T M, Executive Director Member\n6 Dr. Alok Pande, GOI Nominee Director Member\n7 Ms. K Nikhila, RBI Nominee Director Member\n4.4.2 Details of meetings:\nThe Committee held 4 meetings during the period from 01.04.2025 to 31.03.2026 as detailed below:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c757","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":346,"text":"The Committee held 4 meetings during the period from 01.04.2025 to 31.03.2026 as detailed below:\nNumber of Directors Attended\nSl. No. Date of meeting Number of Directors on the Committee\nof Directors (COD Vig)\nthe meeting\n1 26.06.2025 7 7\n2 28.08.2025 6 6\n3 12.12.2025 7 6\n4 12.02.2026 7 7\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n4.5 Stakeholders Relationship Committee of the Board:\nThe Committee was constituted with effect from November 23, 2006 to carry out such functions that are required for\nthe redressal of Shareholders’ and investors’ complaints, including but not limited to transfer of shares, non-receipt\nof dividends, Annual Report and any other grievance that a shareholder or investor of the Bank may have against the\nBank. The Committee was reconstituted from time to time.\n4.5.1 Composition of the Stakeholders Relationship Committee of the Board:\nThe composition of Stakeholders’ Relationship Committee of the Board as on 31.03.2026 stands as under:\nSl. No. Name Chairman/Member\n1 Shri Balmukund Sahay, Part time Non Official Director Chairman\n2 Shri Ashutosh Choudhury, Executive Director Member\n3 Shri Shiv Bajrang Singh, Executive Director Member\n4 Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh, Executive Director Member\n5 Ms. Mini T M, Executive Director Member\n6 Shri Bhupinder Singh Bhalla, Shareholder Director Member\n4.5.2 Function of Stakeholders Relationship Committee of the Board:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c758","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":347,"text":"4.5.2 Function of Stakeholders Relationship Committee of the Board:\nThe role of the committee inter-alia include:\n• Resolving the grievances of the security holders of the Bank including complaints related to transfer/transmission\nof shares, non-receipt of annual report, non-receipt of declared dividends, issue of new/duplicate certificates,\ngeneral meetings etc.\n• Review of measures taken for effective exercise of voting rights by shareholders.\n• Review of adherence to the service standards adopted by the Bank in respect of various services being rendered\nby the Registrar & Share Transfer Agent.\n• Review of the various measures and initiatives taken by the Bank for reducing the quantum of unclaimed\ndividends and ensuring timely receipt of dividend warrants/annual reports/statutory notices by the shareholders\nof the company.\n4.5.3 Details of meetings:\nThe Committee held one meeting during the period from 01.04.2025 to 31.03.2026 as detailed below:\nSl. No. Date of meeting Number of Directors on the Stakeholders’ Relationship Committee\nNumber of Directors Attended\nthe meeting\n1 10.06.2025 6 6\n4.5.4 Compliance Officer:\nShri Dina Nath Kumar, Asst. General Manager & Company Secretary has been designated as Compliance Officer of\nthe Bank.\n4.6 IT Strategy Committee:\nIT Strategy Committee was set up to look into the technological upgradation requirements of the Bank and recommend","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c759","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":347,"text":"IT Strategy Committee was set up to look into the technological upgradation requirements of the Bank and recommend\na strategic plan with clearly defined milestones. The committee is reconstituted from time to time.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n4.6.1 Composition of the IT Strategy Committee (IT Com.):\nThe members of the IT Strategy Committee (ITSC) as on 31.03.2026 were as under:\nSl. No. Name Chairman/Member\n1 Shri Bhupinder Singh Bhalla, Shareholder Director Chairman\n2 Shri Binod Kumar, MD & CEO Member\n3 Shri Ashutosh Choudhury, Executive Director Member\n4 Shri Shiv Bajrang Singh, Executive Director Member\n5 Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh, Executive Director Member\n6 Ms. Mini T M, Executive Director Member\n7 Dr. Alok Pande, GOI Nominee Director Member\n8 Shri Vishvesh Kumar Goel, Part time Non Official Director Member\n9 Shri Balmukund Sahay, Part time Non Official Director Member\nRepresentative of IDRBT, domain expert and IT consultant are Special Invitee to Committee meetings. CISO is also an\ninvitee to the committee.\n4.6.2 Details of meetings:\nThis Committee held 6 meetings during the period from 01.04.2025 to 31.03.2026, as detailed below:\nNumber of Directors Attended\nSl. No. Date of meeting Number of Directors on the IT Strategy\nCommittee of Board\nthe meeting\n1 15.05.2025 9 9\n2 16.06.2025 9 9\n3 12.08.2025 8 8\n4 14.11.2025 8 8\n5 03.02.2026 9 8\n6 17.03.2026 9 9","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c760","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":348,"text":"6 17.03.2026 9 9\n4.7 Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow-up of cases of Frauds (SCBMF) {Previously: Special\nCommittee (Monitoring of Large Value Frauds)}\nRBI came up with a notification DOS.CO.FMG.SEC.No.5/23.04.001/2024-25 dated July 15, 2024, repealing “Special\nCommittee (Monitoring of Large Value Frauds)” and all relevant previous circulars issued by RBI in this regard.\nConsequently, RBI directed for re-constitution of ‘Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow-up\nof cases of Frauds’ (SCBMF). This replaced the Special Committee (Monitoring of Large Value Frauds). In line with\nthe above guideline, Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow-up of cases of Frauds’ (SCBMF) was\nreconstituted on 29.07.2024.\nSCBMF shall oversee the effectiveness of the fraud risk management in the bank and review and monitor cases of\nfrauds, including root cause analysis, and suggest mitigating measures for strengthening the internal controls, risk\nmanagement framework and minimizing the incidence of frauds. Also, the coverage may include categories/trends of\nfrauds, industry/sectoral/ geographical concentration of frauds, delay in detection/classification of frauds and delay\nin examination/conclusion of staff accountability, etc.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c761","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":349,"text":"2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n4.7.1 Composition of Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow-up of cases of Frauds (SCBMF)\n{Previously: Special Committee (Monitoring of Large Value Frauds)}:\nThe members of the Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow-up of cases of Frauds (SCBMF) as on\n31.03.2026 were as under:\nSl. No. Name Chairman/Member\n1 Shri Balmukund Sahay, Part time Non Official Director Chairman\n2 Shri Binod Kumar, MD & CEO Member\n3 Shri Ashutosh Choudhury, Executive Director Member\n4 Shri Shiv Bajrang Singh, Executive Director Member\n5 Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh, Executive Director Member\n6 Ms. Mini T M, Executive Director Member\n7 Dr. Alok Pande, GOI Nominee Director Member\n8 Shri Sanjeev Maheshwari, Shareholder Director Member\n4.7.2 Details of meetings:\nThe Special Committee of the Board for Monitoring and Follow-up of cases of Frauds (SCBMF) held 4 meetings\nduring the period from 01.04.2025 to 31.03.2026 as detailed below:\nNumber of Directors on the Special Committee of the Board\nNumber of Directors Attended\nSl. No.\nDate of meeting\nfor Monitoring and Follow-up of cases of Frauds (SCBMF)\nthe meeting\n1 22.04.2025 8 5\n2 12.08.2025 7 7\n3 12.12.2025 8 6\n4 12.02.2026 8 8\n4.8 Customer Service Committee of the Board:\nThe Customer Service Committee was constituted on August 24, 2004 and was reconstituted from time to time. The","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c762","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":349,"text":"The Customer Service Committee was constituted on August 24, 2004 and was reconstituted from time to time. The\nfunctions of the Customer Service Committee include the following:\n• To look into the simplification of procedures and practices with a view to safeguard the interest of common persons\n• To review the systems in place for providing service to the customers and\n• To review the regulations and procedures prescribed by Reserve Bank of India that impinge on customer service\nof banks.\n4.8.1 Composition of Customer Service Committee of the Board:\nThe members of Customer Service Committee of the Board as on 31.03.2026 were as under:\nSl. No. Name Chairman/Member\n1 Shri Binod Kumar, MD & CEO Chairman\n2 Shri Ashutosh Choudhury, Executive Director Member\n3 Shri Shiv Bajrang Singh, Executive Director Member\n4 Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh, Executive Director Member\n5 Ms. Mini T M, Executive Director Member\n6 Shri Balmukund Sahay, Part time Non Official Director Member\n7 Shri Vishvesh Kumar Goel, Part time Non Official Director Member\nInvitees: Shri Palaniappan S- General Manager (ACoE) (as representative of Divyangjans) and Internal Ombudsman.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n4.8.2 Details of meetings:\nThe Committee held 5 meetings during the period 01.04.2025 to 31.03.2026 as detailed below:\nNumber of Directors Attended","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c763","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":350,"text":"Number of Directors Attended\nSl. No. Date of meeting Number of Directors on the Customer\nService Committee\nthe meeting\n1 17.06.2025 7 6\n2 28.08.2025 6 6\n3 29.11.2025 7 7\n4 19.02.2026 7 6\n5 27.03.2026 7 7\n4.9 Nomination and Remuneration Committee of the Board:\nNomination and Remuneration Committee was constituted in the Bank on 27.11.2019 based on RBI / DFS guidelines\nfor determining the ‘Fit and Proper’ status of persons to be elected as Shareholder Director on the Board. The\nCommittee was reconstituted from time to time.\n4.9.1 Composition of Nomination and Remuneration Committee of the Board:\nThe members of the Remuneration Committee of the Board as on 31.03.2026 were as under:\nSl. No. Name Chairman/Member\n1 Shri Balmukund Sahay, Part time Non Official Director Chairman\n2 Shri Vishvesh Kumar Goel, Part time Non Official Director Member\n3 Shri Sanjeev Maheshwari, Shareholder Director Member\n4 Shri Bhupinder Singh Bhalla, Shareholder Director Member\n4.9.2 Details of meetings:\nThe Committee held 3 meetings during the period 01.04.2025 to 31.03.2026 as detailed below:\nNumber of Directors Attended the\nSl. No. Date of meeting Number of Directors on the NRC\nCommittee\nmeeting\n1 17.06.2025 4 4\n2 30.12.2025 3 3\n3 10.02.2026 4 4\n4.10 Board Committee for Performance Evaluation\nThe committee was constituted on 27.11.2019 for approval of KRAs of GMs, CGMs and EDs and to set up KRAs of MD","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"