.2025\nDemitted office on","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c774","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":357,"text":"Demitted office on\n9. Shri Sujit Kumar Dey Chief General Manager - CRO &\nSuperannuation 01.01.2026\nFRMD\nGeneral Manager, Risk Management\nChief General Manager-Chief Risk\n10. Shri Navin Kumar Shrivastava\nOfficer (CRO) 01.01.2026\nDepartment\n6. Remuneration to Directors:\nThe remuneration including travelling and halting expenses to Non-Executive Directors are paid as stipulated by\nthe Central Government in consultation with Reserve Bank of India from time to time in terms of Clause 17 of the\nNationalized Banks (Management and Miscellaneous Provisions) Scheme, 1970 (as amended).\nThe Managing Director & CEO and Executive Directors (Whole Time Directors) are paid remuneration by way of salary\nas per rules framed by the Government of India. The details of remuneration paid to the Managing Director & CEO\nand Executive Director(s) are as under:\nIncentives\nDearness Allowance\nPF/NPS Bank Contribution\nGrand Total\nTotal\nSl. No. Name Basic Pay\nArrear (Rs.)\n/Other allowances (Rs.)\n(Rs.)\n(Rs.)\n(Rs.)\n(Rs.)\n(Rs.)\n1 Shri S L Jain* 0.00 0.00 0.00 1600080.00 1600080.00 0.00 1600080.00\n2 Shri Binod Kumar 2680000.00 1514392.00 100604.25 682874.48 4977870.73 272500.65 5250371.38\n3 Shri Mahesh Kumar Bajaj# 562800.00 309540.00 11256.00 4922296.67 5805892.67 56280.00 5862172.67\n4 Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh 2688000.00 1518720.00 711375.87 2103600.00 7021695.87 314092.26 7335788.13","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c775","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":357,"text":"4 Shri Brajesh Kumar Singh 2688000.00 1518720.00 711375.87 2103600.00 7021695.87 314092.26 7335788.13\n5 Shri Shiv Bajrang Singh 2688000.00 1518720.00 973923.99 2486913.33 7667557.32 328340.65 7995897.97\n6 Shri Ashutosh Choudhury 2688000.00 1518720.00 1047917.26 2622690.33 7877327.59 717386.37 8594713.96\n7 Ms. Mini TM 948266.67 549994.67 0.00 0.00 1498261.34 94826.67 1593088.01\n*MD & CEO upto 31.12.2024\n#Executive Director upto 30.06.2025\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nAt present, the Bank does not have Stock Option Plan for its Directors.\nThe Salary and incentives paid to the Whole Time Directors are as per Government of India guidelines.\nGovernment of India vide communication dated 30.08.2019 provided flexibility to Boards of Large Public Sector Banks (PSBs) having total business (being the summation of gross loans and advances and total deposit of the Bank, reckoned as per the last declared results of the Bank) of Rs.10 lakh crore or higher, to decide sitting fees payable to Non-Executive Directors subject to an overall ceiling of Rs.25 lakhs per annum.\nFurther, Government of India, Ministry of Finance vide letter no.F.No.15/1/2011-BO.I dated 28.10.2025 communicated that:\n1. There shall be no overall ceiling limit on payment of sitting fee.\n2. The per-sitting amount may be determined by the Board of Directors of respective Public Sector Banks, subject","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c776","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":358,"text":"2. The per-sitting amount may be determined by the Board of Directors of respective Public Sector Banks, subject\nto limitations prescribed under the Companies Act, 2013, and the regulations enacted thereunder.\nAccordingly, Board of Directors of the Bank in its meeting held on 06.03.2026 accorded approval for sitting fees (per\nmeeting) as under:\n1. For attending Board Meeting Rs.90,000.00\n2. For attending meeting of Board level committees Rs.45,000.00\n3. For chairing Board Meeting Rs.10,000.00 (in addition to 1.)\n4. For Chairing meeting of Board level Committees Rs.5,000.00 (in addition to 2.)\nThe Sitting fee is paid to the non-Executive Directors as per the provisions of Nationalized Banks (Management & Miscellaneous Provisions) Scheme 1970, read with Government of India guidelines for attending Board and Board\nCommittee meetings, Details of sitting fee paid during the FY 2025-26 are as under:\nSl. No. Name of the Director (Rs. in Lakh)\n01 Shri Balmukund Sahay 22.85\n02 Shri Vishvesh Kumar Goel 29.10\n03 Shri Pradeep Kumar Malhotra 9.15\n04 Shri Sanjeev Maheshwari 24.95\n05 Shri Bhupinder Singh Bhalla 6.55\nNote: No sitting fee is payable to Whole Time Directors and Directors representing Government of India & Reserve\nBank of India\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n7. General Body Meetings:\n7.1 Particulars of past three Annual General Meetings of the Bank:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c777","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":359,"text":"7.1 Particulars of past three Annual General Meetings of the Bank:\nNatureof Meeting | Dateand Time | Venue | Purpose\nSeventeenth Annual General Meeting | Monday the , 19thJune , 2023 | ThroughVideo Conferencing (VC)/Other AudioVisual Means(OAVM) | 1 Todiscuss approveandadopttheAuditedBalanceSheetoftheBank . , i asatMarch31 2023 theProftandLossaccountfortheyearended , , on that date the Report of the Board of Directors on the working , andactivitiesoftheBankfortheperiodcoveredbytheAccountsand theAuditors’ReportontheBalanceSheetandAccounts . 2 TodeclaredividendonEquitySharesoftheBank . . 3 ToapprovetheappointmentofShriMaheshKumarBajaj Executive . , Director(DIN:08080244) . 4 To approve appointment of Dr Maruthi Prasad Tangirala Non- . . , Executive Director (Government of India’s Nominee Director) (DIN: 03609968) . 5 To raise equity capital aggregating upto Rs4000 Crore (including . . premium)throughQIP/FPO/RightsIssueorin