heBank . 6 ToapproveappointmentofM/s ShanmugamRajendran&Associates . . LLP Company Secretaries as Secretarial Auditor of the Bank for a , i term of fve years from FY 2025 -26 to FY 2029 -30 . 7 To raise equity capital aggregating upto Rs5000 Crore (including . . premium)throughQIP/FPO/RightsIssueorincombinationthereof","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c780","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":359,"text":"7.2 In the 17th Annual General Meeting held on 19th June 2023, a special resolution approving raising equity capital aggregating upto Rs.4000 Crore (including premium) through QIP/ FPO/ Rights issue or in combination thereof was passed. In the 18th and 19th Annual General Meeting held on 15th June 2024 and 17th June 2025 respectively, a special resolution approving raising equity capital aggregating upto Rs.5000 Crore (including premium) through QIP/ FPO/ Rights issue or in combination thereof was passed.\n7.3 No Special Resolution was passed in Extraordinary General Meeting (EGM) or through postal ballot during the financial year 2025-26.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n7.4 The following Directors were present in the last Annual General Meeting of the Bank held on 17.06.2025:\nShri Binod Kumar MD & CEO (in the chair)\nShri Mahesh Kumar Bajaj Executive Director\nShri Ashutosh Choudhury Executive Director\nShri Shiv Bajrang Singh Executive Director\nShri Brajesh Kumar Singh Executive Director\nShri Pradeep Kumar Malhotra Shareholder Director\nShri Sanjeev Maheshwari Shareholder Director and Chairman of Audit Committee of Board\nPart Time Non-Official Director and Chairman of Stakeholders Relationship Committee and Nomination & Remuneration Committee\nShri Balmukund Sahay\nShri Vishvesh Kumar Goel Part Time Non Official Director\n8. Means of Communication:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c781","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":360,"text":"8. Means of Communication:\nThe Bank appreciates the benefit accruing to the society with the advent and advancement of technology and means\nof communications and further recognizes the need of keeping its stakeholders informed of the events of their\ninterest. The quarterly / half yearly / annual financial results of the Bank are submitted to the Stock Exchanges namely,\nNSE and BSE, where the equity shares of the Bank are listed. The Financial Results are published in one national\nnewspaper (English), one national newspaper (Hindi) and one regional language newspaper based at Chennai as per\nstatutory requirement. During the financial year 2025-26, the quarterly / half yearly financial results were published in\nleading newspapers namely “Financial Express, Jansatta (Hindi), Dainik Jagran, Indhu Tamizh Thisai (Tamil), Business\nStandard, English & Hindi edition and Dinamani (Tamil) etc.. The results are also displayed on the website of the Bank\nwww.indianbank.bank.in.\nThe presentation made to the analysts / institutional investors, is also hosted on the Bank’s website, www.indianbank.\nbank.in .\n9. General Shareholders Information:\n9.1 Particulars of 20th Annual General Meeting:\nDay and Date 17 June 2026\nTime 11:00 AM","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c782","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":360,"text":"Time 11:00 AM\nAGM will be held through Video Conferencing (VC)/ Other Audio Visual Means (OAVM), as such, the Bank’s Corporate Office at 254-260, Avvai Shanmugam Salai, Royapettah, Chennai-600014 will be the deemed venue for AGM.\nVenue\n9.2 Financial Year and Calendar for Publication of Financial Results:\nThe Financial Year of the Bank is April to March.\n9.3 Dividend payment date:\nDividend payment date : within 30 days from date of declaration\n9.4 Dividend:\nThe Board of directors of the Bank has recommended a dividend of Rs.18.25 per equity share i.e.182.50% of paid up\nequity capital of the Bank for Financial Year 2025-26.\n9.5 Listing:\nThe equity shares of the Bank are listed with National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. (NSE) and BSE Ltd. (BSE).\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nStock Exchange Stock Code Date of Listing\nNational Stock Exchange of India Ltd. (NSE), Exchange Plaza, Plot No. C.1, G-Block, Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra (E), Mumbai-400051 INDIANB 01.03.2007\nBSE Ltd. (BSE), P. J. Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai - 400 001. INDIANB/532814 01.03.2007\nThe advance Annual Listing fee for the financial year 2026-27 has already been remitted to the above Stock Exchanges.\n9.6 Market Price Data:\nThe monthly high and low quotations and the volume of shares traded on National Stock Exchange of India Ltd.(NSE)","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c783","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":361,"text":"The monthly high and low quotations and the volume of shares traded on National Stock Exchange of India Ltd.(NSE)\nand BSE Ltd. (BSE) during the financial year 2025-26 were as under:\nNSE BSE Total Volume (Nos. in\nVolume (Nos. in\nVolume (Nos. in\nMonth\nHigh (Rs.) Low (Rs.)\nlakh) High (Rs.) Low (Rs.)\nlakh)\nlakh)\nApr-25 599.90 517.85 363.57 599.95 519.50 10.18 373.75\nMay-25 628.95 546.10 471.97 628.70 539.70 20.02 491.99\nJun-25 658.50 606.00 733.61 658.50 609.05 24.14 757.75\nJul-25 657.95 606.00 406.30 658.60 605.55 18.66 424.96\nAug-25 683.10 611.10 250.75 683.00 612.40 10.65 261.40\nSep-25 761.05 653.00 344.24 760.85 653.05 8.76 353.00\nOct-25 879.00 730.60 472.05 878.90 731.00 15.87 487.92\nNov-25 894.85 850.00 313.90 898.60 850.00 7.16 321.06\nDec-25 890.00 764.05 509.65 891.85 764.30 13.23 522.88\nJan-26 923.00 807.80 420.68 923.15 808.0