2220 1.3372\n501 - 1000 5754 1.7602 4273285 0.3173\n1001 - 2000 2192 0.6706 3123166 0.2319\n2001 - 3000 584 0.1787 1448686 0.1076\n3001 - 4000 243 0.0743 862970 0.0641","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c785","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":362,"text":"3001 - 4000 243 0.0743 862970 0.0641\n4001 - 5000 190 0.0581 885314 0.0657\n5001 - 10000 274 0.0838 2001082 0.1486\n10001 & above 627 0.1918 1316357258 97.7277\nTotal 326889 100.00 1346963981 100.00\n9.11 Dematerialization of shares:\nThe Bank's shares are compulsorily traded in demat form. The ISIN code of Bank’s Equity Shares is INE562A01011.\nAs on 31.03.2026, 134,55,90,421 equity shares constituting 99.90% of the equity shares are in dematerialized form.\nParticulars of shares in Demat and Physical form held by the shareholders as on 31.03.2026 are as under:\nNumber of\nShares held in Number of shareholders % of shareholders\n% of shareholding\nshares\nPhysical form 40,081 12.26 13,73,569 00.10\nNSDL 1,45,075 44.38 33,33,96,930 24.75\nDematerialized form\nCDSL 1,41,733 43.36 101,21,93,482 75.15\nTotal 3,26,889 100.00 134,69,63,981 100.00\nThe Equity holding of Govt. of India as on 31.03.2026 is 99,45,49,600 equity shares of Rs.10/- each, which constitutes\n73.84% of the paid up capital of the Bank.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n9.12 There are no outstanding GDRs / ADRs / Warrants or any Convertible instruments as on date.\n9.13 Foreign Exchange Risk and Hedging Activities:\nThe Bank has in place a policy on managing credit risk arising out of Unhedged Foreign Currency Exposures of its","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c786","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":363,"text":"The Bank has in place a policy on managing credit risk arising out of Unhedged Foreign Currency Exposures of its\nborrowers. Where there is no natural hedge, forward cover is suggested to customers in respect of import/export\ntransactions. The forward cover will act as Unhedged risk mitigation on exchange risk. While sanctioning the facilities,\nthe Bank is ensuring that all the exposures (fund based and non-fund based) in foreign currencies are covered by\nforward cover. Request for considering waiver of forward cover if any is considered only at corporate office level. While\nreviewing the borrowal accounts, unhedged exposures are captured and impact is analysed in credit proposals.\nThe Bank has provided a provision of Rs.116.00 crore for the year ended 31st March 2026 on Unhedged Foreign Currency\nExposure to their constituents in terms of RBI Master Direction on Commercial Banks-Credit Risk Management dated\n28th November 2025.\n9.14 Details of Bonds / Debt Instruments issued by the Bank and outstanding as on 31.03.2026:\nDetails of Bonds issued by the Bank and outstanding as on 31.03.2026 are as under:\nName of Credit\nOutstanding\nAmt. (Rs. in crore)\nName & Address of Bond\nRating Agency\nRating as on\nParticulars ISIN\nTrustee\n(ies)\n31.03.2026\nBasel III Compliant Tier 2 Bonds Series III\nINE428A08051 1000","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c787","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":363,"text":"INE428A08051 1000\nAxis Trustee Services Ltd. The Ruby, 2nd Floor, SW 29, Senapati Bapat Marg, Dadar West, Mumbai - 400 028.\nInfrastructure Bond Series I INE562A08099 5000\nCARE Ratings Ltd.\nCARE AAA / Stable CRISIL AAA / Stable\nCRISIL Ratings Ltd.\nInfrastructure Bond Series II INE562A08107 5000\nInfrastructure Bond Series III INE562A08115 5000\nTotal 16000.00\nBesides the Bank has unutilized rating for AT 1 Bonds of Rs.1000 crore (AA+/Stable) and Tier 2 Bonds of Rs.2000 crore (AAA/\nStable) from both CARE and CRISIL Ratings.\nOther Credit Ratings:\nIn addition to the above, the Bank has also obtained Credit Rating for its Certificate of Deposits from CRISIL Ratings and\nissuer rating from S&P Global Ratings and CARE Ratings Ltd. The details are as under:\nName of Credit Rating\nType of Instrument /\nOutstanding Rating\nSl. No.\nAmt. (Rs. in crore)\nAgency (ies)\nType of Rating\nas on 31.03.2026\n1. CRISIL Ratings Ltd. Certificate of Deposits 45000 CRISIL A1+\n2. S & P Global Ratings Issuer Credit Rating - BBB / Stable / A-2\n3 CARE Ratings Ltd. Issuer Credit Rating - AAA/Stable\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n10. Other Disclosures:\n(a) Related party transaction of the Bank are disclosed in the notes to accounts Schedule 18 of the Balance Sheet as on\n31.03.2026. Other than those in the normal course of banking business, the Bank has not entered into any materially","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c788","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":364,"text":"31.03.2026. Other than those in the normal course of banking business, the Bank has not entered into any materially\nsignificant transactions with its Promoter / Directors, Management, their relatives etc. that may have potential conflict\nwith the interest of the Bank at large.\n(b) The Bank has complied with the requirements regarding capital market and no penalty or stricture whatsoever has\nbeen imposed by the Stock Exchanges or SEBI during the last three financial year.\n(c) The Bank being one of the Nationalized Banks, has complied with the requirement of SEBI (Listing Obligations and\ndisclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 to the extent applicable/compliable.\n(d) The Bank has formulated a ‘Policy for determining Material Subsidiary’ and the same is available on Bank’s website,\nwww.indianbank.bank.in.\n(e) The Bank is having two listed subsidiaries namely, Indbank Merchant Banking Services Limited and Ind Bank Housing\nLimited and one unlisted wholly owned subsidiary namely Indbank Global Support Services Ltd. None of them are\n‘material subsidiary of the Bank. Besides three subsidiaries, the Bank also has two joint ventures namely, Universal\nSompo General Insurance Company Ltd. and Asrec (India) Ltd.\n(f) In line with the Sexual Harassment of Women at work place (Prevention, Prohibition and Redressal) Act, 2013 and Rules","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c789","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":364,"text":"(f) In line with the Sexual Harassment of Women at work place (Prevention, Prohibition and Redressal) Act, 2013 and Rules\nmade thereunder, the Bank has formulated a policy for prevention of Sexual Harassment of Women at workplace. The\ndetails of complaints received and resolved during the financial year 2025-26 and pending as on 31.03.2026 are as\nfollows:-\nPending as on\nResolved during FY\n01.04.2025 Received during\n2025-26 Pending as on\nFY 2025-26\n31.03.2026\nNumber of Complaints 04 05 09 0\n(g) A Certificate from a Company Secretary in practice certifying that none of the Directors on the Board of the Bank\nhave been debarred or disqualified from being appointed or continuing as Directors of the Bank by SEBI/Ministry of\nCorporate Affairs or any such Statutory/Regulatory Authority is attached and form part of the report.\n(h) The certificate issued by the Statutory Central Auditors of the Bank, regarding compliance of conditions of Corporate\nGovernance in terms of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 is annexed to\nthis report.\n(i) Total Professional Fee and other expenses paid to Statutory Central Auditors of the Bank for the previous Financial\nYear 2024-25 is Rs.646.08 lakhs.\n(j) A Compliance Certificate from the Managing Director & CEO of the Bank and Chief Financial Officer as stipulated under","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c790","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":364,"text":"(j) A Compliance Certificate from the Managing Director & CEO of the Bank and Chief Financial Officer as stipulated under\nRegulation 33(2) read with Regulation 17(8) of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations,\n2015 has been placed before the Board and is annexed to the Annual Report.\n(k) Commodity price risks and commodity hedging activities - Not Applicable.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n(l) Discretionary requirements:\nThe details regarding adoption of discretionary requirements specified in Part E of Schedule II of SEBI (LODR)\nRegulations, 2015, as amended, is as under:\nRequirement Compliance\nA. Board:\nA non-executive Chairperson may be entitled to maintain a chairperson’s office at the listed entity’s expense and also allowed reimbursement of expenses incurred in performance of his/ her duties.\nNot Applicable\nB. Shareholder rights:\nThe half-yearly results are published in the newspapers, uploaded in Bank’s website and are available on the websites of Stock Exchanges, NSE & BSE.\nA half-yearly declaration of financial performance including summary of the significant events in last six-months, may be sent to each household of shareholders.\nC. Modified Opinion(s) in audit report:\nThe audit report on the financial statements of the Bank for FY 2025-26 has unmodified opinion.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c791","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":365,"text":"The audit report on the financial statements of the Bank for FY 2025-26 has unmodified opinion.\nThe listed entity may move towards a regime of financial statements with unmodified audit opinion.\nD. Separate posts of Chairperson and Managing Director or\nthe Chief Executive Officer:\nPresently the Bank does not have regular Non- Executive Chairperson.\nThe listed entity may appoint separate persons to the post of chairperson and the Managing Director or Chief Executive Officer. such that the Chairperson shall –\nAs per the provisions of Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Act, 1970, the Chairman is appointed by the Government of India.\n(a) be a non-executive director; and\n(b) not be related to the Managing Director or the Chief\nExecutive Officer as per the definition of the term “relative” defined under the Companies Act, 2013\nE. Reporting of internal auditor:\nThe concurrent auditors / inspectors of branches reports are consolidated and placed before the Audit Committee of the Bank periodically.\nThe internal auditor may report directly to the audit committee.\nF. Independent Directors:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c792","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":365,"text":"F. Independent Directors:\nThe independent directors of top 2000 listed entities as per market capitalization shall endeavour to hold at least two meetings in a financial year, without the presence of non- independent directors and members of the management and all the independent directors shall endeavour to be present at such meetings\nTwo meetings of the Independent Directors were held during FY 2025-26 on 19.05.2025 & 06.03.2026.\n(m) Whistle Blower Policy / Vigil Mechanism:\nThe Bank is committed to the highest standards of ethics, integrity and professionalism in all the activities and operations that it conducts and has defined systems and procedures in place to root out corruption, malpractices and abuse of authority by the employees/ officers in the Bank. The Bank encourages an open and transparent system of working and dealings between the members of staff / officers, customers and members of general public coming into contact with the Bank.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c793","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":365,"text":"The Bank comes within the purview of Central Vigilance Commission. As such, the Bank has framed a Whistle Blower Policy in line with the Govt. of India guidelines in this regard. The policy namely ‘Whistle Blower Policy’ aims at quickly spotting aberrations and dealing with it in the shortest possible time. It has been disseminated among the employees and officers of the Bank ensuring them full confidentiality against disclosure of names and protection to the Whistle Blower against any personal vindictive actions such as humiliation, harassment or any other form of unfair treatment or subjecting to any kind of loss on account of his public interest disclosures. The content of the policy is made available on Bank’s website, www.indianbank.bank.in.\nNo personnel of the Bank have been denied access to the Audit Committee.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n(n) Utilization of Fund raised by the Bank through issuance of Long-Term Infrastructure Bond:\nDuring FY 2025-26, the Bank has raised Long Term Infrastructure Bonds aggregating to Rs.5,000 Crore with tenor of\n10 years, at a coupon of 7.15% p.a. through private placement using electronic Bidding platform of BSE (BSE-EBP).\nThe proceeds of the issue have been utilized for funding/refinancing long term projects in infrastructure sub-sectors\nand affordable housing as prescribed by RBI.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c794","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":366,"text":"and affordable housing as prescribed by RBI.\n(o) During the financial year 2025-26, there were no instances where the Board didn’t accept recommendations of the\ncommittee of the Board which were mandatory for according approval by the Board.\n11. The Bank is in compliance with disclosure requirements pertaining to Corporate Governance Report as stipulated\nunder Sub para (2) to (10) of Para C of Schedule V of SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015.\n11.1 The Bank is in compliance with Corporate Governance Requirements specified in Regulations 17 to 27 and clauses\n(b) to (i) of sub regulation 2 of Regulation 46 of the SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015 except composition of Board of\nDirectors, non-availability of Independent Woman Director and non-availability of 50% independent Directors on the\nBoard, as prescribed under SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015.\n12. Dividend Distribution Policy:\nDividend Distribution Policy of the Bank is available on the Bank’s website, under the link https://indianbank.bank.in/\ndepartments/policies/\n13. Share Transfer and Redressal of Investors’ Grievance:\nThe Bank has appointed Cameo Corporate Services Limited as the Registrar and Share Transfer Agent for recording\nthe shareholders’ requests, resolution of investors’ grievances, amongst other activities connected with the change of","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c795","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":366,"text":"the shareholders’ requests, resolution of investors’ grievances, amongst other activities connected with the change of\naddress, transfer / transmission of shares, change of mandate etc. For the convenience of the investors, grievance /\ncomplaints from them are also accepted at the Bank’s Corporate Office in Chennai. Pursuant to extant SEBI guidelines,\ntransfer requests for shares held in physical form are not being processed with effect from 01.04.2019.\nShareholders should contact their Depository Participant (DP) directly for updating the records in case of any\nchange in address and / or Bank mandate (Name of Bank, Address, Account No, MICR Code etc.) for shares held in\nDematerialized form.\nThe shareholders may lodge their requests / complaints either with the Bank’s Registrar and Share Transfer Agent\n(RTA) or with the Bank at the following address:\nThe Company Secretary Investor Services Cell Indian Bank, Corporate Office , 254-260, Avvai Shanmugam Salai Royapettah, Chennai - 600 014. Telephone: 044-28134484/4698 Email: investors@indianbank.bank.in\nCameo Corporate Services Limited (Unit: Indian Bank) P Subramanian Building 1, Club House Road, Chennai – 600 002. Telephone: 044-28460718 Email:investor@cameoindia.com\n13.1 Number of Investor complaints received, resolved and pending:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c796","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":366,"text":"13.1 Number of Investor complaints received, resolved and pending:\nThe shareholders’ complaints received by the Bank are forwarded to Bank’s RTA for redressal. The details of requests\n/ complaints received and resolved during the financial year 2025-26 and pending as on 31.03.2026 are as follows:-\nPending as on\nResolved during\nPending as on\n01.04.2025 Received during\nNumber of Complaints /\nFY 2025-26\nFY 2025-26\n31.03.2026\nrequests\n0 85 84 1*\n* since resolved\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n14. Disclosure with respect to Demat Suspense Account / Unclaimed Suspense Account:\nThe details of unclaimed shares lying in the Demat Suspense Account are as under:\nAggregate number of shareholders and the outstanding shares in the suspense account lying at the beginning of the year i.e. on 01.04.2025\nShareholders - 33 Shares - 3862\nNumber of shareholders who approached listed entity for transfer of shares from suspense account during the year 1\nNumber of shareholders to whom shares were transferred from suspense account during the year 1\nAggregate number of shareholders and the outstanding shares in the Suspense Account lying at the end of the year i.e. 31.03.2026\nShareholders - 32 Shares - 3756\nThe voting rights in respect of the unclaimed / outstanding shares will remain frozen till the claim by the rightful","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c797","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":367,"text":"The voting rights in respect of the unclaimed / outstanding shares will remain frozen till the claim by the rightful\nowner. On the receipt of valid claim from the rightful owner, the shares lying in the Demat Suspense account are\ncredited in the demat account of claimant.\n15. Shareholding Pattern (as on 31.03.2026):\nNo. of Shares\nShareholding\nShareholder Category No. of Shareholders\nheld\n%\nGovernment of India (President of India) -Promoter 1 994549600 73.84\nMutual Funds* 38 184407228 13.69\nForeign Portfolio Investor(FPI) and Foreign Institutional Investor ( FII)* 292 78422443 5.82\nAlternate Investment Funds 19 539776 0.04\nInsurance Companies* 14 53480479 3.97\nFinancial Institutions/ Banks 8 685314 0.05\nResident Individual 296146 27080514 2.01\nBody Corporate 992 1756848 0.13\nDirectors and their relatives 2 400 0.00\nEmployees 14992 4035409 0.30\nClearing Members 6 5783 0.00\nHindu Undivided Family(HUF) 2878 658172 0.05\nNRI 4490 1249926 0.09\nTrust 15 84144 0.01\nCentral Government/ State Government(s)/ President of India - Non Promoter 2 4189 0.00\nUnclaimed shares demat suspense Account 2 3756 0.00\nTotal 319897 1346963981 100.00\n* Consolidated on common PAN basis\n16 Dividend through National Automated Clearing House (NACH):\nNational Automated Clearing House (NACH) is a centralized system implemented by National Payment Corporation","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c798","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":367,"text":"National Automated Clearing House (NACH) is a centralized system implemented by National Payment Corporation\nof India which facilitates direct credit of the dividend amount to the investors into his / her Bank Account. The Bank\nis offering the services to the shareholders with an option to avail the facility for direct credit of the dividend in their\nBank account. However, the Bank account of the shareholders should be in Core Banking Solution (CBS) Branch of\nBank/s.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\n17. Unclaimed Dividend, if any:\nAs per section 10B of Banking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Act, 1970, any money which is\ntransferred to unpaid dividend account and remains unpaid/unclaimed for a period of seven years from the date of\nsuch transfer shall be transferred to \"Investor Education and Protection Fund\" established under section 205C/125 of\nthe Companies Act, 1956/2013.\nPursuant to the directives/guidelines of the Government of India, Ministry of Finance vide their letter No.\nF.No.7/93/2013- BOA dated 21.05.2014, the unpaid and unclaimed dividend amount of the Bank are transferred to\n\"Investor Education and Protection Fund\" of the Central Government in compliance of Section 10B of the Banking\nCompanies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Act, 1970.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c799","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":368,"text":"Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Act, 1970.\nThe shareholders who have not encashed their dividend warrants for Financial Year 2020-21 and onwards are\nrequested to lodge their valid claim(s) with Registrar and Share Transfer Agent, Cameo Corporate Services Limited,\nSubramanian Building, No.1, Club House Road, Chennai - 600 002, along with their Bank details for remittance of\nproceeds of the unpaid dividend warrant/s to them through NEFT/Direct Credit. For FY 2017-18, 2018-19 and 2019-20,\nno dividend was declared by the Bank.\nFurther, in terms of the Banking Laws (Amendment) Act, 2025, the Bank shall transfer, in accordance with the rules\nmade under Section 124 of the Companies Act, 2013, to the Investor Education and Protection Fund established\nunder Section 125 of the said Act, all shares in respect of which dividend has not been paid or claimed for a period of\nseven consecutive years, along with a statement thereof containing the details specified in the said rules;\nAny person whose shares or unclaimed or unpaid money has been transferred to the Investor Education and\nProtection Fund under Sub-section (3), shall be entitled to claim the transfer from the said Fund, in accordance with\nthe rules made under section 124 and Section 125 of the Companies Act, 2013.”","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c800","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":368,"text":"the rules made under section 124 and Section 125 of the Companies Act, 2013.”\nThe details of the Unpaid Dividend Warrants have been made available on Bank’s website www.indianbank.bank.in.\n18. Related Party Transactions:\nThe Bank has not entered into any material related party transaction as defined under SEBI (Listing Obligations and\nDisclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 during FY 2025-26. The policy on dealing with Related Party Transactions\nis available on Bank’s website, www.indianbank.bank.in.\n19. Code of Conduct:\nThe Bank has framed the “Code of Conduct” applicable to the Board of Directors and Senior Management Personnel\nand the same has been adopted by the Board and the same is available on the Bank’s website viz. www.indianbank.\nbank.in.\nThe Board members and senior management have affirmed compliance with the code on annual basis and a\ndeclaration to this effect from the Managing director & CEO of the Bank, forms part of this report.\n20. Certificate of compliance of conditions of Corporate Governance:\nThe certificate issued by the Statutory Central Auditors of the Bank, regarding compliance of conditions of Corporate\nGovernance in terms of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 is annexed.\nFor and on behalf of the Board of Directors\nDate: 29.04.2026 (Binod Kumar)\nPlace: Chennai Managing Director & CEO","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c801","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":369,"text":"Place: Chennai Managing Director & CEO\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nDECLARATION PURSUANT TO PARA- D OF SCHEDULE V OF THE SEBI (LISTING OBLIGATIONS AND DISCLOSURE REQUIREMENTS)\nREGULATIONS, 2015\nIt is hereby declared that the Board Members and Senior Management Personnel of the Bank (i.e. Chief General Managers/\nVertical Head) have affirmed their compliance with the Code of Conduct for the Financial Year ended on 31st March, 2026 in\nterms of Regulation 26 (3) of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015.\nThe said Code of Conduct is available on the Bank’s website, www.indianbank.bank.in.\nDate: 29.04.2026 (Binod Kumar)\nPlace: Chennai Managing Director & CEO\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nAUDITORS’ CERTIFICATE ON COMPLIANCE OF CONDITIONS\nOF CORPORATE GOVERNANCE\nTo,\nThe Members of Indian Bank\nWe have examined the compliance of conditions of Corporate Governance by INDIAN BANK for the Financial year ended\non March 31st, 2026, as stipulated in Regulation 17 to Regulation 27 and Regulation 46(2) (b to i & t) of SEBI (Listing\nObligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015.\nThe Compliance of conditions of Corporate Governance is the responsibility of the Management. Our examination was\nlimited to procedures and implementation thereof, adopted by the Bank for ensuring the compliance of the conditions","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c802","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":370,"text":"limited to procedures and implementation thereof, adopted by the Bank for ensuring the compliance of the conditions\nof the Corporate Governance. It is neither an audit nor an expression of opinion on the financial statements of the Bank.\nOn the basis of the records and documents maintained by the Bank and the information and explanations given to us:\n(a) We certify that the Bank has generally complied with the conditions of Corporate Governance as stipulated in SEBI\n(Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 with exception as mentioned in Para 11.1 of the\nCorporate Governance Report.\n(b) We state that no investor grievance is pending for a period exceeding one month against the Bank, as per the records\nmaintained by the Stakeholders Relationship Committee and as certified by the Registrar and Share Transfer Agent of\nthe Bank.\nWe further state that such compliance is neither an assurance as to future viability of the Bank nor the efficiency or\neffectiveness with which the Management has conducted the affairs of Bank.\nFor M/s Arun K Agarwal & Associates\nFor M/s Dass Gupta & Associates\nFor M/s G Balu Associates LLP\nChartered Accountants\nChartered Accountants\nChartered Accountants FRN: 000376S / S200073\nFRN: 003917N\nFRN: 000112N\nLOKESH KUMAR GARG\nCHANDAN GUPTA\nR RAVISHANKAR\nPartner (M. No. 413012) UDIN: 26413012CUGZLT4348","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c803","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":370,"text":"Partner (M. No. 413012) UDIN: 26413012CUGZLT4348\nPartner (M. No. 547754) UDIN: 26547754CEPGQP9459\nPartner (M. No. 026819) UDIN: 26026819ZNDWME7563\nFor M/s S P A R K & Associates Chartered\nFor M/s Bhatia & Bhatia\nAccountants LLP Chartered Accountants FRN: 005313C/C400311\nChartered Accountants\nFRN: 003202N\nNILESH GUPTA\nRAVINDER BHATIA\nPartner (M. No. 406020) UDIN: 26406020AATEMP5038\nPartner (M. No. 017572) UDIN: 26017572FZAZOQ6226\nDate: 29.04.2026\nPlace: Chennai\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nCOMPLIANCE CERTIFICATE BY CEO AND CFO\n{Pursuant to Regulation 33 (2) read with Regulation 17 (8) of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015}\nTo,\nThe Board of Directors\nIndian Bank\nThis is to certify that:\n(a) We have reviewed financial statements of Indian Bank for the FY 2025-26 and that to the best of our knowledge and\nbelief:\n(i) these statements do not contain any materially untrue statement or omit any material fact or contain statements\nthat might be misleading;\n(ii) these statements together present a true and fair view of the Bank’s affairs and are in compliance with existing\naccounting standards, applicable laws and regulations.\n(b) There are, to the best of our knowledge and belief, no transactions entered into by the Bank during year, which are\nfraudulent, illegal or violative of the Bank’s Code of Conduct.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c804","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":371,"text":"fraudulent, illegal or violative of the Bank’s Code of Conduct.\n(c) We accept responsibility for establishing and maintaining internal controls for financial reporting and that we have\nevaluated the effectiveness of internal control systems of the Bank pertaining to financial reporting and we have\ndisclosed to the auditors and the Audit Committee, deficiencies in the design or operation of such internal controls, if\nany, of which we are aware and the steps we have taken or propose to take to rectify these deficiencies.\n(d) We have indicated to the Auditors and the Audit Committee:\n(i) that no significant changes in internal control over financial reporting have been made during the Fourth Quarter\nand FY 2025-26 ended on March 31, 2026;\n(ii) that there have been no significant changes in accounting policies during the FY 2025-26 ended on March 31,\n2026 as compared to those followed in preceding Financial Year 2024-25.\n(iii) Instances of significant fraud of which we have become aware and the involvement therein, if any, of the\nmanagement or an employee having a significant role in the Bank’s internal control system over financial\nreporting.\n(Sunil Jain) Chief Financial Officer\n(Binod Kumar) Managing Director & CEO\nPlace: Chennai\nDate: 29.04.2026\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nSECRETARIAL AUDIT REPORT For the Financial Year 2025-26 Ended 31st March, 2026\nTo,","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c805","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":372,"text":"To,\nThe Members,\nINDIAN BANK\n66, Rajaji Salai,\nChennai 600 001.\n(v) The following Regulations and Guidelines prescribed\nWe have conducted the Secretarial Audit of the compliance\nunder the Securities and Exchange Board of India\nof applicable statutory provisions and the adherence to\nAct, 1992 (“SEBI Act”), to the extent applicable: -\ngood corporate practices by Indian Bank [hereinafter\ncalled ‘the Bank’] for the financial year ended 31st March,\n(a) The Securities and Exchange Board of\n2026 [“period under review”]. The secretarial audit was\nIndia (Listing Obligations and Disclosure\nconducted in a manner that provided us a reasonable\nRequirements) Regulations, 2015;\nbasis for evaluating the corporate conduct/statutory\n(b) The Securities and Exchange Board of India\ncompliances and expressing our opinion thereon.\n(Substantial 