res or convertible bonds or convertible debentures or units of equity oriented mutual funds;\nNIL NIL\nix) Financing to stockbrokers for margin trading; NIL NIL\nx) All exposures to Venture Capital Funds (both registered and unregistered) 173.41 190.06\nTotal exposure to capital market 2819.87 2444.58","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c926","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":436,"text":"Total exposure to capital market 2819.87 2444.58\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\nc. Risk category-wise country exposure\n(` in Crore)\nProvision held as at\nProvision held as at\nRisk category Exposure (Net) as\n31.03.2026 Exposure (Net) as\nat 31.03.2026\nat 31.03.2025\n31.03.2025\nInsignificant 24921.38 - 19814.45 12.57\nLow 9928.43 - 7847.27 -\nModerately Low 9.95 - 789.87 -\nModerate 475.91 - 517.13 -\nModerately High 34.11 - 595.17 -\nHigh 1643.86 - 0.61 -\nVery High 0.00 - 636.71 -\nTotal 37013.64 - 30201.21 12.57\nCOUNTRY RISK MANAGEMENT:\nThe Bank has analysed its net funded exposure to various countries as on 31.03.2026 and such exposure to all countries is\nwithin 1% of the total assets of the Bank. Hence the provision of Country Risk for the Bank as on 31.03.2026 is NIL.\nDetails of Single Borrower Limit (SBL), Group Borrower Limit (GBL), if any, exceeded by the Bank\nPercentage of total\nBorrower Name Additional Exposure Total Highest\nPercentage of additional exposure\nExposure\nexposure\nNIL\nd. Letter of comfort issued by the Bank:\nDuring the year ended 31.03.2026 branches in India have not issued any letter of comfort for financing of imports.\nOutstanding as on 31.03.2026 is NIL. Accordingly, there is no financial impact.\nDuring the year ended 31.03.2026, Letter of Comfort issued by our foreign branches (Singapore and Colombo) and","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c927","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":436,"text":"During the year ended 31.03.2026, Letter of Comfort issued by our foreign branches (Singapore and Colombo) and\nGIFT City Branch is NIL and Outstanding as on 31.03.2026 is NIL.\nAs per the Letter of Responsibility given by the Bank to the Monetary Authority of Singapore, Bank to ensure that\nSingapore Branch maintains sound liquidity and a sound financial position at all times. Accordingly, the Bank continues\nto maintain deposits to the extent of USD 43.00 Mio (equivalent to INR 407.79 crore) with Singapore Branch.\nBank has issued LOU for Sri Lankan branches favouring Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL) as per the mandatory\nrequirement of CBSL. Bank undertakes to provide funds as may be necessary to meet all obligations incurred in or in\nconnection with its business in Sri Lanka. Bank does not anticipate any financial impact in immediate near future on\naccount of this LOU.\nBank has issued LOC for our IBU/ FBU in IFSC, SEZ Gift City, Gujarat Favouring International Financial Service Centres\nAuthority (IFSCA) as per the mandatory requirement of IFSCA. Bank undertakes to provide the necessary financial\nassistance as and when required in the form of Capital and liquidity support for our IBU/FBU in IFSC, GIFT city. Bank\ndoes not anticipate any financial impact in immediate near future on account of this LOC.\n2025-26 वाार्षिVिक रिRपाेे(र्टट Annual Report\ne. Unsecured advances\n(` in Crore)","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c928","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":437,"text":"(` in Crore)\nParticulars 2025-26 2024-25\nTotal unsecured advances of the bank 104126.22 70610.23\nOut of the above, amount of advances for which intangible securities such as charge over the rights, licenses, authority, etc. have been taken NIL NIL\nEstimated value of such intangible securities NIL NIL\nf. Factoring exposures:\nThe Banks factoring exposures as at 31st March 2026 is NIL. (Previous Year: NIL)\ng. Intra-group exposures\n(` in Crore)\nSl. No. Particulars 2025-26 2024-25\n1 Total Amount of intra group exposures 1080.63 1311.85\n2 Total Amount of top 20 intra group exposures 1080.63 1311.85\n3 Percentage of intra group exposures to total exposure of the bank on borrowers / customers 0.12% 0.17%\n4 Details of breach of limit on intra group exposures and regulatory action thereon, if any NIL NIL\nh. Unhedged foreign currency exposure\nThe Bank has in place a policy on managing credit risk arising out of Unhedged Foreign Currency Exposures of its\nborrowers. Where there is no natural hedge, forward cover is suggested to customers in respect of import/export\ntransactions. The forward cover will act as Unhedged risk mitigation on exchange risk. While sanctioning the facilities,\nBank is ensuring that all the exposures (fund based and non-fund based) in foreign currencies are covered by forward","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c929","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":437,"text":"Bank is ensuring that all the exposures (fund based and non-fund based) in foreign currencies are covered by forward\ncover. Request for considering waiver of forward cover if any is considered only at corporate office level. While reviewing\nthe borrowal accounts, unhedged exposure are captured and impact is analysed in credit proposals.\nThe Bank has provided a provision of Rs.116 Crore and Capital of Rs.36.08 Crore for the year ended 31st March 2026\non Unhedged Foreign Currency Exposure to their constituents in terms of RBI Master Direction on Commercial Banks-\nCredit Risk Management dated 28th November,2025.\n6. Concentration of deposits, advances, exposures and NPAs\na) Concentration of Deposits\n(` in Crore)\nParticulars As on 31.03.2026 As