ndia,\nparent.\nwhich comprises statutory provisions, regulatory\n/ Reserve Bank of India guidelines, accounting","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1015","section":"Balance Sheet (Consolidated)","tag":"balance","page":487,"text":"/ Reserve Bank of India guidelines, accounting\nb. The Subsidiaries, Joint Ventures and Associates\nstandards / guidance notes issued by the Institute\nfollow Accounting Policies as prescribed by the\nof Chartered Accountants of India and the practices\nrespective regulatory authorities and as per\nprevalent in the Banking Industry in India. In respect\nstatutory requirements. In view of such diverse\nof foreign branches as per statutory provisions and\naccounting policies required to be followed,\npractices prevailing in the respective countries.\nthe consolidated financial statements have\nbeen prepared by adopting the respective\n2. USE OF ESTIMATES :\naccounting policies of the mandated / statutory\nThe preparation of financial statements requires the\nrequirements.\nmanagement to make estimates and assumptions\nc. The difference between the cost to the parent\nfor considering the reported assets and liabilities\nof its investment in subsidiary entity and the\n(including contingent liabilities) as on the date of\nparent’s portion of its equity in the subsidiary\nfinancial statements and the income and expenses\nwith reference to the date of acquisition\nfor the reporting period. Management believes that\nis recognized in the consolidated financial\nthe estimates used in the preparation of the financial\nstatement as Capital Reserve/Goodwill. The\nstatements are prudent and reasonable.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1016","section":"Balance Sheet (Consolidated)","tag":"balance","page":487,"text":"statements are prudent and reasonable.\nparent’s sh